---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../components/Byline.astro";
import DualDoors from "../components/DualDoors.astro";
import LegalNote from "../components/LegalNote.astro";
import { FROZEN } from "../lib/frozen";
import { LINKS, CANON_PATHS, linkClass, ext } from "../lib/links";
import { withBase } from "../lib/base";

const path = "/sell-through-vs-search-intent";
const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "What sold vs what they asked", path },
];
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sell-through vs search intent | FFL Intel"
  description="A same-store unit is true. A zero-hit search is also true. Only one of those is in Gearfire’s monthly print. Research by Betsy is the third sensor."
  path={path}
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.copilot}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-400 mb-3">
      The ask
    </p>
    <h1 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white text-balance mb-4">
      Sell-through vs search intent
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 mb-6">
      One number is what rang. The other is what they tried to find. Stapling
      them is how a Monday meeting goes wrong.
    </p>
    <Byline dateLabel="August 13, 2026" read="5 min" />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800">
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.copilot)}
        alt="Betsy — demand research"
        width="1792"
        height="1008"
        class="w-full object-cover object-top max-h-80"
      />
    </figure>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-zinc-300 font-serif">
      <p>{FROZEN.doctrine}</p>
      <p>
        A same-store unit is true. A zero-hit search is also true. Only one of
        those is in Gearfire’s monthly print. March, minus 11.9 percent,
        Outdoor Wire, 13 April. This desk will not invent a Live percentage
        and set it next to that number as if it had a competing index. The
        print cannot see the ask. That is the whole distinction.
      </p>
      <p>
        Last month’s sell-through is last season’s map. Useful. Late. The
        scout is the sentence someone typed when nothing on the shelf answered
        back. Zero-hit demand never becomes a unit. It still happened.
      </p>
      <p>
        Research behind this desk is the third sensor — GunSearchEngine,
        GunSearchAgent embeds, Betsy Live as a labeled sample. Disclosed.
        Not a rival monthly. Frozen: {FROZEN.betsy}
      </p>
      <p>
        Brand teams:{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.brandIntel} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >Brand Intelligence</a
        >
        {" · "}
        <a href={LINKS.copilot} class={linkClass} {...ext}>Co-Pilot</a>.
        Retailers:{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.gsa} class={linkClass} {...ext}>GunSearchAgent</a>.
        Encyclopedia:{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.fortress} class={linkClass} {...ext}>RetailBI vs Betsy</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
    <DualDoors />
    <p class="mt-10"><LegalNote /></p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
